00:27:20.900 --> 00:27:52.050
<v Clevins Browne>I remember leaving the apartment, and everything just looked new to me. In front of my project building there was a sign that says "Hi, you're stepping into Louis H. Pink Houses." And that's a sign I see every single day, but that one day it just looked new to me. I felt older. I just felt like, there's no one here. There's no one that's going to do things for me from this moment on. I have to find out some way to do things on my own.
<v Clevins Browne>我记得离开公寓，一切对我来说看起来都是新的。在我的项目大楼前有一块牌子写着“嗨，你正步入Louis H. 粉红之家。”那是我每天都能看到的牌子，但那天它对我来说看起来很新。我觉得自己变老了。我只是觉得，这儿没别人。从这一刻起，没有人在为我做事。我得想办法自己做每一件事。

00:27:52.050 --> 00:27:55.100
<v Sarah Koenig>So you didn't want any of your neighbors to know you were there.
