00:30:01.460 --> 00:30:41.230
<v Clevins Browne>It really was difficult for me to adjust to the fact that my mother's not here. There's no one for me to talk to. Where is she at at this very moment? Is she OK at this very moment? Is she thinking about me at this very moment? And, at times, I would even listen to radio stations that my mother would listen to, even though I totally hated them. They'd play old music from way back in the day. Sugarfly honey bunch. They played The Temptations and all this stuff. So while my mother was gone, I'd just start listening to WBLS. That's the best way I could really make the house lose its emptiness.
<v Clevins Browne>适应我妈妈不在身边的事实对我来说真的很难。没人跟我说话。她此刻在哪儿？她现在还好吗？她现在在想我吗？有时，我甚至会听我妈妈会听的广播电台，尽管我完全讨厌它们。它们播放来自很久以前的老歌。Sugarfly honey bunch。她们播放The Temptations和所有那些东西。所以当我妈妈离开时，我就开始听WBLS。这是我能真正让房子失去空虚感的最好方式。

00:30:41.230 --> 00:31:09.400
<v Clevins Browne>So I really had no money in the house and everything. So [? Everoll ?] and I and a couple of our friends were walking in the street one day, and we found this garbage bag that had boxes of cigarettes inside there. So I have a stick, a little twig, that I'm just walking by, dragging it along the fence. So I see the garbage bag and I started poking it, and just started poking the bag and everything. So then, all these cigarettes, I don't know where they came from, just fall out of the bag.
<v Clevins Browne>所以我家里真的没钱，什么都没有。所以[? Everoll ?]和我还有我们的一些朋友有一天在街上走，我们发现了这个垃圾袋，里面有几盒香烟。所以我有一根棍子，一根小树枝，我只是走着，沿着栅栏拖着它。所以我看到了垃圾袋，我开始戳它，只是开始戳袋子等等。然后，所有的这些香烟，我不知道它们从哪儿来的，就从袋子里掉了出来。

